Classifier on a *scalar* text:
```
def classify_direction(text):
    t = re.sub(r"\[rev\d+:[^\]]*\]", "", text)  # strip revision history notes
    t = re.sub(r"'strictly STRONGER'", "", t)     # strip quoted historical
    t = re.sub(r"corrected from[^.;]*", "", t)
    strong = re.search(r"strictly\s+stronger", t, re.I)
    weak = re.search(r"strictly\s+weaker", t, re.I)
    predicate_subject = re.search(r"reading|predicate", t, re.I) and not re.search(r"outside|not contained|no single|negation", t, re.I)
    negation_subject = re.search(r"outside|not contained|no single|negation|lies in the union", t, re.I)
    ...
```
Rules:
- if strong and predicate_subject and not negation_subject → INVERTED_IF_PREDICATE_READING (hard)
- if strong and negation_subject → CORRECT_AS_NEGATION_STRENGTH (the negation is stronger)
- if strong → CORRECT_AS_CLASS_STATEMENT_UNSCOPED (needs scoping)
- if weak → okay (predicate-scoped weaker statement): if predicate_subject → CORRECT_PREDICATE_WEAKER
- none → NO_DIRECTION_WORD.

For delta:22 the text contains "the SET-based reading ... it is implied by, and strictly stronger than, the single-q tail predicate" → predicate_subject True ("reading"), negation_subject: does the text contain "outside|not contained|no single|negation|lies in the union"? The full `to` text: "...iff gamma([0,T)) is contained in the union of J^-(q) ... it is implied by, and strictly stronger than, the single-q tail predicate." No negation keywords → INVERTED. 

For map:200 scalar (the class description): text = "... Visibility uses the single-q TAIL predicate: ... The set-based reading (gamma contained in the union of J^-(q) over all q in I+) is strictly stronger; it is registered as variant `SET`..." → predicate_subject True; negation_subject: contains "no future-inextendible causal geodesic ... is visible"? The description earlier says "no future-inextendible causal geodesic of finite affine length is visible from I+" — contains "no " but my regex has "no single" not "no ". So negation_subject False → INVERTED (hard). But wait — the class description's direction word attaches to the *predicate* ("The set-based reading ... is strictly stronger") → yes inverted. Good.

For supplement D1 f0_reading text: "visibility = every incomplete causal geodesic lies outside J^-(I+) as a SET (strictly stronger)" → negation_subject True ("outside") → CORRECT_AS_NEGATION_STRENGTH. Good.

For registry strength (now weaker): weak + predicate_subject ("parent's single-q tail predicate") → CORRECT_PREDICATE_WEAKER.
